    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483">

                <pb facs="0651" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg559"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 800.24/49a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-06T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3148. Your 3082, January 23, 3 p.m., and 3143, February 4, 6 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d483-f1"/> Secretary of War has been consulted and he approves
                    Department’s instruction to you to confer with General Pershing and to request him to assign one of his staff
                    to attend conference mentioned. Report whom General
                        Pershing designates.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d483-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d483-f1" n="1" xml:id="d483-f1-content">
                <p>The latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d483-f2" n="2" xml:id="d483-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 3530 from the Ambassador in France, Apr. 5, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg562">p. 562</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
